    <DataNode elementId="MONOMER-14913" textLabel="(E)-beta-caryophyllene/beta-elemene synthase" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="Q6ZJL3" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="642.791015625" centerY="933.2229614257812" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="O-28, pujar">A cDNA clone was isolated from Oryza sativa. The cDNA was functionaly expressed in vitro and in transgenic Arabidopsis plants. The gene encoded a terpene synthase that catalyzed the formation of volatile sesquiterpenoids Betacary, alpha humulene and beta-elemene. Its expresion followed a circadian rhythm and was expressed in higher quantitites in response to Methyl jasmonate treatment and wound induction |CITS: [17524436]|.</Comment>
