    <DataNode elementId="CPD-8230" textLabel="(-)-β-caryophyllene" type="Metabolite">
      <Xref identifier="NPNUFJAVOOONJE-GFUGXAQUSA-N" dataSource="InChIKey" />
      <Graphics centerX="1062.8291015625" centerY="834.90869140625" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="3955e7" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="3955e7" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="PMN, nilo-poyanco, SRI, caspi">(-)-&amp;beta;-Caryophyllene is a natural bicyclic sesquiterpene that is a constituent of many essential oils, especially clove oil, the oil from the stems and flowers of Syzygium aromaticum, the essential oil of hemp Cannabis sativa, and rosemary Rosmarinus oficinalis. It is usually found as a mixture with isocaryophyllene (the cis double bond isomer) and &amp;alpha;-humulene (obsolete name: &amp;alpha;-caryophyllene), a ring-opened isomer.</Comment>
